15. AI Platform Engineer interview questions
Try answering these verbally.
Q1. What is an LLM API?
An LLM API allows an application to send input prompts to a hosted language model and receive generated responses through an HTTP interface.
Q2. What is the difference between a prompt and a completion?
A prompt is the input provided to the model. The completion or generated output is the model's response.
Q3. What is token usage?
Token usage measures the amount of text processed by the model. It includes input tokens and output tokens and is important for monitoring API consumption and costs.
Q4. Why do you use a separate LLM service layer?
It separates model execution from API routing. This makes it easier to maintain, test and replace model providers without rewriting the API endpoints.
Q5. How would you support multiple LLM providers?
I would introduce a common provider interface and separate implementations for OpenAI, Anthropic and Google. A model registry or routing service would select the appropriate provider based on configuration and request requirements.
Q6. What happens if the OpenAI API becomes unavailable?
The application should handle provider errors, enforce timeouts, retry transient failures with backoff, log failures and return a controlled error to the client. For production systems, I would also consider circuit breakers and fallback providers.
Q7. How would you monitor LLM costs?
I would record provider, model, input tokens, output tokens, request duration and request status. I would then calculate cost using the applicable model-specific pricing and build user-level and organization-level usage dashboards.
